 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Let it cool overnight in the sink or yard, or carry it out on day you leave and let it soak in the sun. Yes, it helps. Washing it in sink with a little soap and cool water is the fastest way to get out dirt and grime. Dig a little shallow trench for them at one corner of the site, near the toilet. Pack them in layers, with the flats on top. It' a big pot, and you probably use it every day, so it' worth treating well. You' be a pro in no time. Just don't burn the bottom, it takes hours to cool.",
